msgid "(the ``ports.public`` protocols the reverse proxy listens on and publishes in host mode, through ``lookup('stream_relay_ports')``) and ``subnet`` (the relay network's block, taken from the role subnet pool like ``local.subnet``). All three are required. While the switch is true and the reverse proxy's own overlay applies in the mode, the provider and the reverse proxy join ``<entity>-relay`` and no other role does, independent of ``modes`` and ``topology``. The provider carries its entity name as alias there. That network is not a role network: :func:`compute_external_network_roles` leaves it out, so neither the pre-created role overlays nor ``proxy_hops`` change with the switch. A switch that is on in a mode of ``UNPROVEN_STREAM_RELAY_MODES`` fails every network lookup of the provider and the reverse proxy."
