msgid "**An agent can be provisioned with its own platform user account.** Creating an agent employee optionally provisions a dedicated identity through the platform's existing user mechanism (the `users` lookup, LDAP via [`svc-db-openldap`](../../roles/svc-db-openldap/), SSO via [`web-app-keycloak`](../../roles/web-app-keycloak/)); no new account system is built. The account is a **non-privileged standard user** by default (never administrator/service-account-with-mutating-tools). When enabled, the agent authenticates as its own user: OIDC login to its dashboard, a distinct mailbox/identity, and MCP calls made with `auth_subject: user` ([050](050-mcp-role-integration.md)) scoped to that account rather than a shared service account. The account is opt-in per agent; its password/token lives in the role's `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:` block, never in README or env. An agent MUST also be deployable against an existing account (no forced account creation)."
msgstr ""

