# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A `Dockerfile.j2` with **Jinja2 control-flow logic** emits a **warning only**. The warning signals that the file should be reviewed to see whether the logic can be eliminated and the file migrated."
msgstr "A ya `Dockerfile.j2` Pamoja na **Jinja2 Udhibiti wa mtiririko** Kutoa A **Tahadhari pekee**Ishara za onyo kwamba faili inapaswa kupitiwa ili kuona kama mantiki inaweza kuondolewa na faili imehamia."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A `Dockerfile.j2` with **no Jinja2 control-flow logic** causes a **test failure**. It MUST be migrated to `files/Dockerfile` with `ARG` declarations."
msgstr "A ya `Dockerfile.j2` Pamoja na **ya ya Jinja2 Udhibiti wa mtiririko** Sababu ya A **Jaribio la kushindwa**Ni lazima kwa ajili ya kuhamia `files/Dockerfile` Pamoja na `ARG` taarifa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A `SYSTEM_EMAIL_<KEY>` variable defined in inventory, group vars, or host vars. No such file ships with the project. This form is an escape hatch for site-specific overrides."
msgstr "A ya `SYSTEM_EMAIL_<KEY>` Tofauti inayofafanuliwa katika hesabu, vars ya kikundi, au vars ya jeshi. Hakuna meli za aina hiyo zilizo na mradi huo. Fomu hii ni hatch ya kutoroka kwa overrides maalum za tovuti."

msgid "A ``# variant-pin:`` in ``R#i`` is in force only while ``R`` is in the include running variant ``i``, and no pin moves a primary app."
msgstr ""

msgid "A ``#fragment`` such as ``#issuecomment-1`` may follow the number. A query, a port, credentials or a deeper path may not. The contributor guide is ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/upstream.md``."
msgstr ""

msgid "A ``container`` hook pipes its script into a command inside the application’s container, for applications whose image ships a scripting runtime. A ``host`` hook runs its script with the node’s Python beside its modules and reaches the container through ``$RBAC_SYNC_CONTAINER_BIN exec ... $RBAC_SYNC_CID``, for applications that only expose a CLI or an HTTP API inside the container. A hook runs on the node of the one container it names and reaches nothing else: in swarm no ``ports.local`` port is published, so an application whose hook acts on its database cannot also call its own HTTP API from there. Such work runs at deploy time inside the application’s network namespace, as `web-app-peertube <../web-app-peertube/README.md>`__ creates its accounts, and the hook keeps the SQL."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A ``database = '*'`` row dumps a whole instance with ``pg_dumpall``. It goes back through ``baudolo-restore cluster`` with the instance's superuser; its ``\\connect`` lines name the databases, while the consumers sit in the compose project of the engine, so both are checked."
msgstr "A ya ``database = '*'`` Spika akitoa mfano wa jumla wa ``pg_dumpall``. Inarudi kupitia ``baudolo-restore cluster`` kwa mujibu wa Ibara ya Rasimu ya Katiba; na ``\\connect`` mistari jina databases, wakati watumiaji kukaa katika kitabu mradi wa injini, hivyo wote ni checked."

