msgid "Act job containers: [workflow.sh](../../../scripts/tests/deploy/act/workflow.sh) wires the folder under the condition `01_bootstrap.sh` uses for the swarm lab nodes, a set variable and an existing `infinito-package-cache-frontend` container. It mounts the folder into every job container it starts, sets `PIP_CACHE_DIR` and blanks `cache: pip` in the copy of the workflow it hands to act, so `actions/setup-python` neither archives the folder after a job nor extracts an old archive into it, and the `make install-force` of each job reuses the wheels the host already downloaded. The deploy workflows on GitHub runners never call the wrapper. The workspace suite ([call-test-workspace.yml](../../../.github/workflows/call-test-workspace.yml)) does, through `make swarm-zombie`, and there too the act jobs get the folder exactly when the lab nodes of the same run get it: whenever the suite's own cache stack is up at that point."
