msgid "For the managed Claude and Codex setup, keep LiteLLM as the client endpoint. Every deploy reads the unified key FreeLLMAPI issued through the authenticated `/api/settings/api-key` endpoint and persists it in the token store for `platform_administrator`. Select both roles and deploy them: LiteLLM publishes `freellmapi/auto` with that key and validates the upstream. Clients continue using LiteLLM virtual keys, not this upstream key. Regenerating the key in the dashboard takes effect with the next deploy of both roles. See [the LiteLLM integration](../svc-ai-litellm/README.md#optional-freellmapi-upstream) for automatic routing, capability declarations and protocol validation. Do not run FreeLLMAPI's client setup commands over the Infinito-managed client configuration, or configure FreeLLMAPI to forward back to LiteLLM."
msgstr ""

msgid "For the managed Claude and Codex setup, keep LiteLLM as the client endpoint. Every deploy reads the unified key FreeLLMAPI issued through the authenticated ``/api/settings/api-key`` endpoint and persists it in the token store for ``platform_administrator``. Select both roles and deploy them: LiteLLM publishes ``freellmapi/auto`` with that key and validates the upstream. Clients continue using LiteLLM virtual keys, not this upstream key. Regenerating the key in the dashboard takes effect with the next deploy of both roles. See `the LiteLLM integration <../svc-ai-litellm/README.md#optional-freellmapi-upstream>`__ for automatic routing, capability declarations and protocol validation. Do not run FreeLLMAPI’s client setup commands over the Infinito-managed client configuration, or configure FreeLLMAPI to forward back to LiteLLM."
