msgid "GraphQL mutations bypass the REST-path-based deny rules entirely. A `mutation { … }` can achieve write effects (label manipulation, project-item creation, issue transfers, etc.) whose REST equivalents are denied by path. The whole endpoint is asked regardless of query direction because `gh api` cannot distinguish a read query from a mutation at the command line; body-flag ask rules also fire for graphql invocations that pass `-f query=…`, providing defence in depth."
msgstr "Mabadiliko ya GraphQL hupita sheria za kukataa msingi wa REST-path kabisa. A ya `mutation { … }` Inaweza kuwa na athari za kuandika (Udhibiti wa lebo, uumbaji wa mradi, uhamisho wa suala, nk.) Na anaye potea basi anapotea kwa khasara ya nafsi yake. Kila kitu kinaulizwa bila kujali mwelekeo wa kuuliza kwa sababu `gh api` hawezi kutofautisha swala la kusoma kutoka kwa mabadiliko katika mstari wa amri; mwili-flag kuuliza sheria pia moto kwa uchochezi graphql kwamba kupita `-f query=…`, kutoa ulinzi kwa kiwango cha juu."

