# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "MUST NOT be deactivated from the `Plugins -> Must-Use` admin screen."
msgstr "Haipaswi kuondolewa kutoka kwenye `Plugins -> Must-Use` Usimamizi wa screen."

msgid "MUST NOT be enabled as a dependency of any other role, another EOL role included: no `meta/services.yml` block, no variant pin, and no `meta/addons/*.yml` whose `bridges:` list names it. The `eol` status carries the `retired` flag, and a retired role may be referenced only by itself and by a `migrations` pair in `meta/lifecycle.yml` (`web-app-stalwart` importing `web-app-mailu`). The `eol-dependency` rule enforces all three, and `INFINITO_LIFECYCLES` is why: the envelope drops an EOL role from every CI round under the default envelope, so the dependency binds a partner no test deploys and first surfaces on a production host as an unreachable integration. An explicit `lifecycles: eol` workflow dispatch deploys the role standalone, and the literal flags keep every partner unbound even in that round."
msgstr ""

msgid "MUST NOT be named by any other role's role id either: no `run_after` or `required_by` entry, no `meta/main.yml` dependency, no `include_role`/`import_role`, no `'<role>' in group_names` gate and no `lookup(..., '<role>', ...)`. The `lifecycle-reference` rule ([test_lifecycle_references.py](../../../../../tests/lint/ansible/roles/meta/test_lifecycle_references.py)) enforces it; a case that cannot leave yet carries `# nocheck: lifecycle-reference` with a `Reason:`."
msgstr ""

msgid "MUST NOT be pinned truthy by any variant in any `meta/variants.yml`, its own included, neither under `services:` nor under `addons:`. A variant pin re-enables the role for that round alone, which is the one place where neither the banner nor the stored flag is in view."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "MUST NOT be placed in a subdirectory, because WordPress does not recurse into `mu-plugins`."
msgstr "Haipaswi kuwa chini ya uongozi, kwa sababu WordPress Hakuna kurudi nyuma katika `mu-plugins`..."

msgid "MUST NOT be referenced by a role whose status carries the `production` flag (`beta`, `rc`, `stable`): `deprecated` sorts beyond every production status, and the upstream `main` runs production roles ship from never deploy it. The `lifecycle-reference` rule enforces it."
msgstr ""

