msgid "The Infinito.Nexus API is a public, read-only REST service built with `FastAPI <https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/>`__. It answers every question an app built on Infinito.Nexus asks about the platform: which roles exist, what their metadata says, how they are categorised, which bundles combine them, what the history of the repository and its forks looks like, and how all of that reads in each of the 184 ISO 639-1 languages."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Infinito.Nexus GUI store reads the same `meta/forms.yml` to prefill and edit these fields before the deploy; its requirement 061 in the GUI repository follows this standard."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Infinito.Nexus licence governs this repository's own code. It says nothing about the software a role deploys, and that is where a restriction on commercial use usually sits. This page answers, per role, what the deployed software's own licence allows."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Joomla plugin keeps overwriting the user's groups from Keycloak on every login; locking the profile fields belongs to requirement 072."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The Keycloak **Userinfo** preview for the user contains a `groups` array with the full path. If it does not, the scope is not reaching the userinfo endpoint and the mapping will not fire."
msgstr "Kwa kuwa Keycloak **Mtumiaji** Maelezo ya mtumiaji ina `groups` Weka katikati ya mtihani. Ikiwa haifanyi, upeo haufiki mwisho wa mtumiajiinfo na ramani haitawaka moto."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The Keycloak OIDC client for ERPNext is **auto-provisioned** via `web-app-keycloak`, consistent with every other OIDC-consuming role in the repo."
msgstr "Kwa kuwa Keycloak Kampuni ya OIDC kwa ajili ya ERPNext Ilikuwa ni **Uwasilishaji wa auto** Kwa kupitia `web-app-keycloak`, sambamba na majukumu mengine yote ya OIDC katika repo."

msgid "The Keycloak group tree behind these paths is materialised by a per-application group-ldap-mapper (roles/web-app-keycloak/tasks/update/03_per_app_mappers.yml), anchored at `/<group_root>/<application_id>` with `group.name.ldap.attribute=description`."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The Keycloak group tree is built by **per-application** `group-ldap-mapper`s. Each deployed application gets one mapper anchored at `/roles/<application_id>` whose LDAP filter `(&(objectClass=groupOfNames)(cn=<application_id>-*))` surfaces only that application's role groups. The mapper uses the LDAP `description` attribute as the visible Keycloak group name, so the resulting group paths carry no redundant prefix."
msgstr "Kwa kuwa Keycloak Mradi wa ujenzi wa kituo hicho umeandaliwa na **Matumizi ya** `group-ldap-mapper`s. kila maombi yaliyotumiwa hupata ramani moja iliyounganishwa kwenye `/roles/<application_id>` Jinsi ya kutumia filter `(&(objectClass=groupOfNames)(cn=<application_id>-*))` Inaunganisha tu makundi ya kazi ya maombi hayo. Mtumiaji huyu anatumia mtandao wa LDAP `description` Kuwa kama inayoonekana. Keycloak Jina la kikundi, kwa hivyo njia ya kundi linalosababisha njia hazibeba prefix."

msgid "The Keycloak username pattern accepts both forms; the OpenLDAP length constraint becomes `IAM_ACCOUNT_MAX_LENGTH`. Only the provisioner creates names that contain `0`; the deploy and the reaper disable and report every account of the agent form without a provisioner record."
msgstr ""

msgid "The LDAP `filter_string` has no Playwright test for admitting a member on the native login form or through its administrator branch: with `sso` off no Keycloak exists to write a group membership to the directory, and the trusted-header bridge evaluates the filter only when it provisions an account, which `test-rbac-gate.js` spends on the user-group branch; options: an LDAP write helper in the persona library, or a second test persona."
msgstr ""

msgid "The LDAP federation sets ``trustEmail: true``: a user the federation imports for the first time is marked verified, because the directory is the platform’s own and seeded from the inventory. An entry an LDAP tool (LAM, phpLDAPadmin) creates with an address is trusted the same way. Keycloak applies it only at the first import, so every deploy with LDAP and ``verifyEmail`` extends the same trust to the users imported earlier: before the settings converge turns ``verifyEmail`` on, ```files/python/email_verified.py`` <files/python/email_verified.py>`__ with ``FEDERATION`` marks every user linked to the realm’s LDAP provider with a non-blank address verified (``tasks/update/06_users/email_federated.yml``). Local users without that link stay as they are, because their unverified state is what ``verifyEmail`` exists to catch. Inventory users are also marked verified at every deploy while ``services.keycloak.users.emails_verified`` is on (the default); any other local user confirms its address once through the link."
msgstr ""

msgid "The LDAP federation sets `trustEmail: true`: a user the federation imports for the first time is marked verified, because the directory is the platform's own and seeded from the inventory. An entry an LDAP tool (LAM, phpLDAPadmin) creates with an address is trusted the same way. Keycloak applies it only at the first import, so every deploy with LDAP and `verifyEmail` extends the same trust to the users imported earlier: before the settings converge turns `verifyEmail` on, [`files/python/email_verified.py`](files/python/email_verified.py) with `FEDERATION` marks every user linked to the realm's LDAP provider with a non-blank address verified (`tasks/update/06_users/email_federated.yml`). Local users without that link stay as they are, because their unverified state is what `verifyEmail` exists to catch. Inventory users are also marked verified at every deploy while `services.keycloak.users.emails_verified` is on (the default); any other local user confirms its address once through the link."
msgstr ""

msgid "The LDAP variant's group mapping (`web-app-jenkins-<role>` groups under the roles OU) is asserted only through the role-strategy assignment (`rbac: the LDAP realm grants each Jenkins role to its directory group`), not by a member signing in. Cause: the LDAP-only variant deploys no Keycloak, so a spec has no path to put biber into a directory group. Options: give the Playwright runner an LDAP write path (an `ldapmodify` helper or the `web-app-lam` API) and add a developer-membership scenario for the LDAP realm."
msgstr ""

msgid "The LLM is wired to the shared LiteLLM gateway when `LITELLM_USABLE`. `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is not used."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Laravel debug bar is rendered on every page while `services.snipe-it.debug.enabled` is on, because `templates/env.j2:5` maps it onto `APP_DEBUG`. Options: set `DEBUGBAR_ENABLED=false` in `templates/env.j2`, or keep `APP_DEBUG` off and raise only the log level."
msgstr ""

msgid "The LdapSource task in `tasks/01_manager_ops.yml` now masks its output with `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS`, because its environment carries `LDAP_BIND_PW`; Playwright cannot observe a deploy log, so no spec covers it. Options: a lint that requires `no_log` on every task whose `environment:` reads `LDAP.BIND_CREDENTIAL`."
msgstr ""

msgid "The MCP path authenticates with a static key, not with the platform identity. Tracked separately if wanted."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The MCP surface ships disabled by default and is independent of the host role's `lifecycle`: a `beta` host role MUST NOT imply that its MCP surface is stable. An MCP surface is only considered validated once its acceptance criteria are met end to end."
msgstr "Meli za uso wa MCP zimezimwa kwa default na zinajitegemea jukumu la mwenyeji. `lifecycle`: A: ya ya `beta` Jukumu la mwenyeji haipaswi kuashiria kwamba uso wake wa MCP ni imara. Uso wa MCP unachukuliwa tu kuthibitishwa mara tu vigezo vyake vya kukubalika vinafikia mwisho."

msgid "The MDAD bootstrap wait in `tasks/flavor/ansible/06_proxy_wiring.yml` (line 7 to 14) is nearly exhausted: a cold bootstrap took about 24 minutes in a compose baseline of 2026-10-09 and used 287 of its 360 retries at 5 s, while the task name still says \"cold ~10-15min\"; options: raise `retries` to about twice the measured time (about 580) and name the measured duration."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The MDAD inventory is templated to enable a conservative-default bridge set plus Jitsi + Element Call. Bridge enablement is gated on `lookup('config', application_id, 'services.matrix.plugins.<bridge>')`. v1 default-ON set (operator-confirmed): `mautrix_signal`, `mautrix_telegram`, `mautrix_twitter`, `mautrix_slack`, `appservice_irc`, `heisenbridge`, `discord`, `gitter`, `hookshot`. Default-OFF (operator opts in): every bridge that needs a third-party API token the operator must obtain manually — `facebook`, `instagram`, `googlechat`, `mautrix_whatsapp`, `sms`, `appservice_kakaotalk`, and the superseded `mx_puppet_{slack,discord}`."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The MariaDB image tag to pull (e.g. `10.6`, `10.11`, or `latest`)."
msgstr "Kwa kuwa MariaDB Picha kwa ajili ya kuvuta (ya g. `10.6`, Kwa hivyo, `10.11`, Kwa hivyo, au `latest`)..."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The Matomo API token is generated during the Matomo bootstrap and persisted to disk by `sys-token-store`. It is then resolved through `lookup('users')`, which hydrates tokens from the store at runtime."
msgstr "Kwa kuwa Matomo API Vifaa hivyo vinatolewa wakati wa Matomo Bonyeza hapa na kuendelea na download `sys-token-store`. Baada ya hapo utajibiwa kwa `lookup('users')`, ambayo huingiza mbegu kutoka kwenye mbegu."

# (Mahitaji ya Mahitaji 025) kujengwa juu ya template umoja kutunga, na full
# Docker-in-Docker kutengwa, jeshi-mtandao mode cascaded kwa addons na Jitsi,
# kati Postgres backend kugawana MATRIX_POSTGRES variables, na coturn ya kati
# inayoendana na vigezo vya pamoja vya coturn kwa jukumu la MASH. Picha ya
# mgombea wa MDAD (wa wa wa wa 3.13Kuwa na docker 28.0.4 Uhamiaji, Uhamiaji
# wathibitishwa dhidi ya V2026.05.18.0) Inaweka CA ya Infinito iliyosainiwa
# ndani ya mkimbiaji na Synapse, na bootstrap sasa inarudi safi kutoka kwa
# alama ya stale.
msgid "The Matrix role gains an ansible flavor (requirement 025) built on a unified compose template, with full Docker-in-Docker isolation, host-network mode cascaded to the addons and Jitsi, a central Postgres backend sharing the MATRIX_POSTGRES variables, and a central coturn aligned to the shared coturn variables for the MASH role. A dedicated MDAD runner image (python 3.13-slim with docker 28.0.4 CLI, migration validated against v2026.05.18.0) mounts the Infinito self-signed CA into both the runner and Synapse, and bootstrap now recovers cleanly from a stale marker."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Miniflare stores are SQLite files, so the role pins itself to the manager node, keeps its volumes off NFS and runs one replica of each service."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Multisite variant in [meta/variants.yml](meta/variants.yml) sets `rbac.tenancy.axis: domain`, declares `network-administrator` and `site-owner` with `scope: global`, keeps `mcp` global and declares the `domains.served` parent of the `site-owner` sites. [rbac_group_map.json.j2](templates/rbac_group_map.json.j2) builds every group path with `rbac_group_path` and hands the map to the mu-plugin as `WORDPRESS_RBAC_GROUP_MAP`. A deploy that enables Multisite without `rbac.tenancy.axis: domain` fails in [tasks/00_core.yml](tasks/00_core.yml) with a message naming the missing tenancy, before the role deploys anything."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Multisite variant in `meta/variants.yml <meta/variants.yml>`__ sets ``rbac.tenancy.axis: domain``, declares ``network-administrator`` and ``site-owner`` with ``scope: global``, keeps ``mcp`` global and declares the ``domains.served`` parent of the ``site-owner`` sites. `rbac_group_map.json.j2 <templates/rbac_group_map.json.j2>`__ builds every group path with ``rbac_group_path`` and hands the map to the mu-plugin as ``WORDPRESS_RBAC_GROUP_MAP``. A deploy that enables Multisite without ``rbac.tenancy.axis: domain`` fails in `tasks/00_core.yml <tasks/00_core.yml>`__ with a message naming the missing tenancy, before the role deploys anything."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The NGINX Certbot Automation role ensures that Let's Encrypt SSL/TLS certificates stay valid without manual intervention. It enhances the security and reliability of web services by automating certificate lifecycle management."
msgstr "Kwa kuwa NGINX Certbot Automation Jukumu la kuhakikisha kwamba tunaruhusu vyeti vya SSL / TLS kubaki halali bila kuingilia mwongozo. Inaongeza usalama na kuaminika kwa huduma za wavuti kwa kuendesha usimamizi wa maisha ya cheti."

