msgid "The broker MUST receive `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username` and `X-Forwarded-Email` from `oauth2-proxy`, and keys every account on `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username` alone: it never reads `X-Forwarded-User`, which carries the e-mail address. On a user's first authenticated visit the broker calls the PDS `com.atproto.server.createAccount` endpoint with a synthesised app-password, encrypts that password with AES-256-GCM under a key from the project's credentials vault, and records handle, DID and ciphertext in the broker volume keyed by Keycloak username. Subsequent visits, also after a broker restart, decrypt the stored password in-broker, exchange it for a PDS session via `com.atproto.server.createSession`, and seed `localStorage[\"BSKY_STORAGE\"]` so the social-app finds an authenticated session at boot. The handle is the username without prefix, `i8-<username>` for a name the PDS reserves, and a handle the user picks in a form when the username exceeds the PDS limit of 18 characters."
msgstr ""

