msgid "The cutover is covered end to end by [`files/test/test.sh`](files/test/test.sh), which runs as this role's CLI test whenever `web-app-mailu` is co-deployed in compose. The whole scenario runs inside the deployed host and needs nothing from the environment around it: it stores mail in both directions in the legacy Mailu, seeds a mailbox that is no inventory user (with a subfolder, flags, a fixed internal date and an active Sieve script), a mailbox in a domain Stalwart does not serve and, in matrix **variant 1**, a mapped mailbox, runs [`files/python/migrate_from_mailu.py`](files/python/migrate_from_mailu.py) with the argv a real cutover uses, and asserts over IMAP and JMAP that everything arrived where it belongs, that the Sieve script files new mail, that the foreign domain was not created and that a second run imports nothing. No redeploy is involved; the cutover is a docker-level data move."
