# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The narrow case is what a deploy job actually sees, because the matrix hands every row exactly one kind. Reading that narrowness as a demand would turn every condition the applying step tolerates into a red row on every deploy: a loop device it could not claim, a pool another job still holds. The run's own input decides instead."
msgstr "Kesi nyembamba ni nini kazi ya kupeleka kweli anaona, kwa sababu mikono ya tumbo kila mstari hasa aina moja. Kusoma kuwa nyembamba kama mahitaji ingeweza kugeuka kila hali ya kutumia hatua kuvumilia katika mstari mwekundu juu ya kila kupeleka: kifaa kitanzi haikuweza kudai, bwawa kazi nyingine bado ana. Matokeo ya uchaguzi wenyewe ndiyo haya."

msgid "The native ``root`` account signs in with the **first 50 characters** of the platform administrator’s password, not the whole secret. PeerTube caps a user password at 50 characters and 72 bytes (``CONSTRAINTS_FIELDS.USERS.PASSWORD``, “Limited by bcrypt algorithm”), and a declared user’s password is 64 characters: handed over in full, ``/api/v1/users/token`` answers ``too_long_password`` and ``npm run reset-password`` refuses it with “New password is invalid.”. ``PEERTUBE_ROOT_PASSWORD`` in `vars/main.yml <./vars/main.yml>`__ is the single place that bounds it; the deploy, the design token and ``templates/playwright.env.j2`` all read it from there. Signing in through Keycloak uses the full password."
msgstr ""

msgid "The native `root` account signs in with the **first 50 characters** of the platform administrator's password, not the whole secret. PeerTube caps a user password at 50 characters and 72 bytes (`CONSTRAINTS_FIELDS.USERS.PASSWORD`, \"Limited by bcrypt algorithm\"), and a declared user's password is 64 characters: handed over in full, `/api/v1/users/token` answers `too_long_password` and `npm run reset-password` refuses it with \"New password is invalid.\". `PEERTUBE_ROOT_PASSWORD` in [vars/main.yml](./vars/main.yml) is the single place that bounds it; the deploy, the design token and `templates/playwright.env.j2` all read it from there. Signing in through Keycloak uses the full password."
msgstr ""

msgid "The native administrator's password does not converge: `tasks/04_native_admin.yml` calls `com.atproto.server.createAccount` on every deploy and treats `400 Handle already taken` as success, so on an existing account a rotated `users.administrator.password` never reaches the PDS and `createSession` (native admin test, design spec sign-in) fails with the new value. Options: after the 400, probe `createSession` and on 401 set the password through `com.atproto.admin.updateAccountPassword` with the PDS admin credentials in the request body."
