# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "This role installs the [sudo](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudo) package and deploys a default sudoers file to ensure secure and consistent privilege escalation on the target system. It uses a preconfigured sudoers file that follows best practices and includes directives to read drop-in files from `/etc/sudoers.d`."
msgstr "Jukumu hili linajumuisha [ya sudo](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudo) mfuko na kupeleka default sudoers faili ili kuhakikisha usalama na thabiti upendeleo kupanda kwenye mfumo lengo. Inatumia faili iliyosimamiwa ambayo inafuata mazoea bora na inajumuisha maagizo ya kusoma faili za kushuka kutoka kwenye faili. `/etc/sudoers.d`..."

msgid "This role installs the ``app-control`` command, writes its configuration, renders the paused page, and, on hosts that also deploy ``web-app-semaphore``, creates the restricted account the Semaphore runner signs in as. The server stage installs all of this once its roles are deployed and before the E2E run; the last step of every deploy applies the persisted pause state of every application on the host. ``sys-svc-compose`` registers each compose instance with it, and the vhost hook in ``sys-front-inj-all`` answers a paused application with HTTP 503 and the paused page."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role installs the ``baudolo`` CLI, lays out the on-host backup tree, deploys the systemd service that drives the periodic run, and wires the cleanup-of-failed-backups dependency so partial snapshots are not retained. Database seeding for individual apps is contributed by the consumer roles via ``tasks/03_seed-database-to-backup.yml``, which they include conditionally once ``svc-bkp-volume-2-local`` is in ``group_names``. The first seed of a play reads ``databases.csv`` once through ``tasks/05_read-seeded-databases.yml``; a consumer whose row already holds its credentials skips ``baudolo-seed``, every other consumer still calls it at its own point in the play. ``baudolo-seed`` gets the password on stdin (``--password-stdin``), so it never shows in the host’s process list."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role installs the `app-control` command, writes its configuration, renders the paused page, and, on hosts that also deploy `web-app-semaphore`, creates the restricted account the Semaphore runner signs in as. The server stage installs all of this once its roles are deployed and before the E2E run; the last step of every deploy applies the persisted pause state of every application on the host. `sys-svc-compose` registers each compose instance with it, and the vhost hook in `sys-front-inj-all` answers a paused application with HTTP 503 and the paused page."
msgstr ""

msgid "This role installs the `baudolo` CLI, lays out the on-host backup tree, deploys the systemd service that drives the periodic run, and wires the cleanup-of-failed-backups dependency so partial snapshots are not retained. Database seeding for individual apps is contributed by the consumer roles via `tasks/03_seed-database-to-backup.yml`, which they include conditionally once `svc-bkp-volume-2-local` is in `group_names`. The first seed of a play reads `databases.csv` once through `tasks/05_read-seeded-databases.yml`; a consumer whose row already holds its credentials skips `baudolo-seed`, every other consumer still calls it at its own point in the play. `baudolo-seed` gets the password on stdin (`--password-stdin`), so it never shows in the host's process list."
msgstr ""

