msgid "Those three ask whether the application is *served* over the self-signed CA. An application that only *calls* one resolves no mode of its own and would be skipped, so a service may declare ``ca_client: true`` and be answered on the deployment's TLS mode, or on an SSO issuer that resolves self-signed TLS. Either peer is enough: the object store a container signs media against and the issuer it authenticates through are different hosts, and answering for only one leaves the other's handshake unverifiable. Without the CA such a container verifies against an empty trust store and fails every outbound call at the TLS handshake."
