# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Two log-parsing trip-wires shape the regexes below. The non-skip status match is anchored to line start (after optional indent) so a substring in arbitrary task output cannot fake a status. And Ansible's `log_path` file (`ANSIBLE_LOG_PATH`, what the swarm/compose deploy feeds this verifier) prefixes every line with `<ts> p=<pid> u=<user> n=<name> <LVL>| `; left unstripped that prefix defeats both the line anchor and the `\\nTASK [` block split, so every required role would false-positive as \"did not execute\"."
msgstr "Vipande viwili vya karatasi za karatasi za rangi ya rangi ya chini. Mechi ya hali ya sikip imewekwa kwa mstari kuanza (Baada ya kuingia) Kwa hivyo kulazimisha katika matokeo ya kazi ya kiholela haiwezi kudanganya hali. Kuwa na wasiwasi `log_path` Faili ya faili (`ANSIBLE_LOG_PATH`, Je, ni aina gani ya mazao ya mazao ya kilimo/mazabibu yanayozalisha mazao haya) Inaunganisha kila mstari na `<ts> p=<pid> u=<user> n=<name> <LVL>| `; kushoto unstripped kwamba prefix kushindwa wote line na na `\\nTASK [` Kuvunjika kwa kizuizi, kwa hivyo kila jukumu linalohitajika litakuwa la uongo kama \"Hakufanya mauaji\"..."

msgid "Two mechanical consequences follow and are implemented with it. `format` travels with a request instead of being pinned to `text` in the LibreTranslate backend, because a tag sent in text mode is translated rather than preserved, and it joins the cache key so a text-mode answer is never served to an html-mode request. A caller may name protected spans of its own alongside the Weblate glossary, because a masked placeholder is not a glossary term and a prompted backend has no html mode to protect it with."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Two of those data-plane dependencies have a central Infinito.Nexus service equivalent — [`svc-db-mariadb`](../../roles/svc-db-mariadb/) and [`svc-db-redis`](../../roles/svc-db-redis/) — and MUST be reused per the central-service convention. Frappe's three Redis logical roles are served by a single central Redis instance using distinct DB numbers (Frappe supports that out of the box via `redis_cache` / `redis_queue` / `redis_socketio` config entries)."
msgstr "Mbili kati ya hizo zenye uwezo wa kubeba mzigo wa Infinito.Nexus Kiwango cha huduma - [`svc-db-mariadb`](../../roles/svc-db-mariadb/) Aidha, na [`svc-db-redis`](../../roles/svc-db-redis/) - na inapaswa kutumika tena kwa mkataba wa huduma kuu. Tatu ya Frappe Redis Kazi za msingi zinafanywa na mtu mmoja Redis Kutumia nambari tofauti za DB (Magufuli akichangia jambo hilo kupitia `redis_cache` Kwa hivyo `redis_queue` Kwa hivyo `redis_socketio` Ingia kwa kuingia)..."

# kumbukumbu ya kichwa *Aidha, na* Tawi la kichwa, kwa misingi tofauti,
# haiwezi kuambiwa mbali na mzigo wa malipo ya kukimbia: uendeshaji wa PR ya
# fork hubeba tupu `pull_requests` ya ya ya ya ya ya ya `head_branch` Na kwa
# upande wa `head_sha`. Msaidizi huyo aliuliza API Ikiwa ombi lolote la kuvuta
# la wazi linashiriki kichwa hicho, na huacha mchezaji wa tawi wakati mtu
# anafanya - kufuta kitu chochote cha kufuta kufuta ombi la kuvuta vibaya.
# Kama hiyo lookup yenyewe inashindwa matcher anakaa juu, kwa sababu kushindwa
# lookup ni zaidi uwezekano kuliko kichwa pamoja.
msgid "Two open pull requests that share a head repository *and* a head branch, to different bases, cannot be told apart from the run payload: the runs of a fork PR carry an empty `pull_requests` array, the same `head_branch` and the same `head_sha`. The helper therefore asks the API whether any other open pull request shares that head, and drops the branch matcher while one does — cancelling nothing beats cancelling the wrong pull request. If that lookup itself fails the matcher stays on, because a failed lookup is far more likely than a shared head."
msgstr ""

