msgstr ""

msgid "Under `all` dnsmasq drops to `user=dnsmasq`, and the deploy requires that user. Upstream DNS for direct names is admitted only for the effective UID of the running dnsmasq, read from `/proc/<MainPID>/status`. The deploy refuses that UID when it is 0 or 65534 or when processes other than dnsmasq run as it, because the admission would cover them too."
msgstr ""

msgid "Under `all` nothing on the host resolves beside dnsmasq: `resolve` leaves the `hosts:` line of nsswitch.conf; systemd-resolved, where present, gets a drop-in with `DNS=127.0.0.1`, an empty `FallbackDNS=` and `Domains=~.`; resolv.conf loses the clearnet nameserver; the docker daemon gets the bridge as its only resolver, because Docker moves on to the next nameserver on the SERVFAIL dnsmasq answers while Tor is down; and the deploy refuses `server`, `resolv-file`, `servers-file` and `conf-file` lines in `/etc/dnsmasq.conf`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Under `all` the forward chain ends in its own `drop` and jumps nowhere, so no rule returns into a chain without one. Both chains accept local IPv6, and the output chain accepts IPv6 neighbour discovery."
msgstr ""

msgid "Under `all`, outbound SMTP and any other non-TCP traffic to unlisted destinations is dropped; add the MX hosts to `direct.include` when the node needs them. Time sync works against the pre-filled servers and the names below them only, and Tor itself needs a correct clock."
msgstr ""

