msgid "[x] A unit test proves that the drift report hides the values of every field the fail-closed rule of decision 5 does not clear, and never repeats a source that did not resolve. `drift` in `utils/roles/applications/forms.py` shows old and new values only for a field that declares a type from `SHOWN_TYPES`, whose source is a dotted path outside `users` and `secrets.credentials`, has no segment matching `SECRET_SEGMENT` (`pass|secret|token|key|pin|credential|bind|pw|salt|bearer|webhook`, any case) or naming a declared credential (any case), resolves in the unrendered application passed as `raw_application` to a plain scalar without `{{` or `{%`, and whose old and new values are a plain `str`, `int`, `float`, `bool` or `None` that holds no URL userinfo and contains no string of `secret_values` (the `credentials` and `secrets.credentials` leaves of every application and every `users.<key>.password`). Without `raw_application` or `secrets` no value is shown, and without a resolved source the line names only `<form>.<field>`. `TestDriftShowsOnlyPlainValues`, `test_no_drift_line_carries_a_secret_value` and `test_without_the_raw_application_or_the_secrets_nothing_is_shown` in `tests/unit/python/utils/roles/applications/test_forms.py` prove each rule with synthetic secrets, including the skeptic's probe cases (an int PIN, `credentials.pin`, `services.ldap.bind_password`, `SMTP_PASSWORD`, an untyped `None -> secret`, a mapping, a `str` subclass, `services.kix.admin_pw`, `auth_salt`, `mcp.bearer`, `webhook_url`, a `database.url` with `postgres://u:<secret>@`, a JWT- and a SendGrid-shaped source that does not resolve, a templated raw value, and a raw value that is no plain scalar). `test_a_plain_setting_shows_both_values` and the second halves of the raw-template, URL-userinfo, known-secret and declared-credential tests are the negative controls."
msgstr ""

