msgid "[x] Once `container_ports` publishes no loopback port in swarm, a lint fails for every swarm-rendered `container_ports` term that carries `DOCKER_BIND_HOST` and no exemption, and a second lint fails for every host-side task or `templates/*.env.j2` that reads a `ports.local` port or `DOCKER_REACH_HOST`, or names a bare loopback host and a local port in separate values, without a compose gate or an exemption. A term is exempt when a vhost reaches its `(service, protocol)` through `proxy_pass`, when it renders only outside swarm (a compose-only Jinja branch, `compose_mode_force: compose`) or when it feeds Discourse's `expose:` list; a read is exempt behind a `when:` or include site that only mode variables confine to compose. Every other term and read carries `nocheck: swarm-loopback-port <exec|overlay|netns|unused|open> <reason>`, `open` citing the open criterion that tracks it as `NNN :LINE`, and a marker that covers nothing fails as dead. (`tests/lint/ansible/jinja/test_swarm_loopback_port_terms.py` and `tests/lint/ansible/tasks/test_swarm_loopback_port_consumers.py`, both green, on `utils/roles/swarm_loopback.py` and `utils/roles/swarm_loopback_reads.py`; each has a fixture negative control. The `open` markers list the remaining host-side reaches of the two criteria above, among them the central Postgres and MariaDB init under variant 0, which sets `exposed: true`.)"
