# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Home Assistant scopes the token to the account that minted it. This deployment mints it for the administrator, so a call arrives as the administrator whoever asked the client. Entity exposure still bounds the reach. Getting to the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Msaidizi wa nyumbani anapanua ishara kwenye akaunti ambayo iliipunguza. Kupelekwa hii mints kwa msimamizi, hivyo wito fika kama msimamizi yeyote aliuliza mteja. Ufichuzi wa hisia bado una mipaka ya kufikia. Kuingia kwenye seva ya chombo imefungwa kwenye jukumu ``mcp`` Kikundi cha RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattermost bounds a call by the account the token belongs to. This deployment mints that personal access token for the administrator account, so calls arrive with that account’s rights whoever asked. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Hata hivyo, wito huo umezua mjadala mkali. Kupelekwa hii mints kwamba binafsi upatikanaji ishara kwa akaunti ya msimamizi, hivyo wito kuwasili na haki ya akaunti hiyo mtu yeyote aliuliza. Kufikia seva ya chombo imefungwa kwenye jukumu ``mcp`` Kikundi cha RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the personal access token is minted against the ``root`` account and stored under the ``administrator`` key, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering GitLab."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Alama ya upatikanaji wa kibinafsi imepunguzwa dhidi ya ``root`` Akaunti na kuhifadhiwa katika ``administrator`` Muhimu, hivyo kila simu hubeba haki za akaunti hiyo bila kujali ni nani aliyeuliza mteja. Kufikia seva ya chombo imefungwa kwenye jukumu ``mcp`` RBAC, ambayo ni ruzuku tofauti kutoka kwa kusimamia GitLab..."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the web-service token is issued against the administrator account, so a call carries that account’s rights regardless of who asked the client. The attached functions are read-only, which bounds what those rights can do here. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Ishara ya huduma ya wavuti imetolewa dhidi ya akaunti ya msimamizi, kwa hivyo simu hubeba haki za akaunti hiyo bila kujali ni nani aliyeuliza mteja. Kazi zilizowekwa ni za kusoma tu, ambazo zina mipaka ya haki hizo zinaweza kufanya hapa. Kufikia seva ya chombo imefungwa kwenye jukumu ``mcp`` Kikundi cha RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``. A call arrives at Baserow as the endpoint owner regardless of who asked the client, and reaches only the one workspace that account owns. That is the second bound under the adapter’s allowlist, not a substitute for it."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``. Wito wa kuwasili Baserow Kama mmiliki wa mwisho bila kujali ni nani aliyeuliza mteja, na anafikia tu nafasi moja ya kazi ambayo akaunti inamiliki. Hiyo ni awamu ya pili chini ya ruhusu ya adapta, sio mbadala."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from holding a Nextcloud account."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` Chama cha RBAC, ambacho ni ruzuku tofauti kutoka kwa kushikilia Nextcloud Akaunti ya."

msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``: the API token is issued against the MCP credential owner, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. ``templates/casc.yaml.j2`` grants that account the ``viewer`` role, or the ``developer`` role while ``mcp.tools.mutating_tools_enabled`` is on. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering Jenkins."
