msgid "``native``: while ``sso`` is on and both ``native`` and ``ldap`` are off, Element’s ``sso_redirect_options`` (``on_welcome_page``, ``on_login_page``) hand its welcome and sign-in pages straight to Keycloak, so Element never renders the password form. Synapse keeps password login on its client API, because the platform administrator, the bot accounts and the role-group reconcile sign in with local passwords. The form is shared: local and LDAP accounts sign in through the same Element form, and native off cannot refuse local accounts while LDAP stays on."
msgstr ""

