# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``tools_unenforceable`` is that same rule applied to the tool policy rather than the connection. A client filters by tool name, so a provider that resolves no callable name gives it nothing to pin and the rendered filter would be empty. That happens two ways, and neither is a working pairing: a surface composed at runtime keeps its contract in ``tools.categories``, which no per-tool filter can express, and a surface that withholds every tool it serves as mutating has nothing left to offer. Advertising either as a configured server would leave an agent wired to a provider it can never call."
msgstr "``tools_unenforceable`` Sheria hiyo inatumika kwa sera ya chombo badala ya uhusiano. Kichujio cha mteja kwa jina la chombo, kwa hivyo mtoa huduma ambaye anatatua jina lolote la simu haitoi chochote cha kupiga na kichujio kilichotolewa kitakuwa tupu. Hiyo hutokea njia mbili, na wala si jozi ya kazi: uso linajumuisha wakati wa kukimbia unaweka mkataba wake katika. ``tools.categories``, ambayo hakuna kichujio cha kila mahali kinaweza kuonyesha, na uso unaozuia kila chombo kinachotumika kama kubadilika hauna chochote cha kutoa. Matangazo ama kama seva iliyosanidiwa ingeacha wakala wired kwa mtoa huduma ambayo haiwezi kupiga simu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``tools``:           ``allowlist`` is what a reader may reach and ``writer_allowlist`` what a writer may reach; the deployment renders one contract per role, each with its own bearer, because the gateway tells callers apart by credential and by nothing else. ``allowlist`` is policy, what the platform lets a consumer reach, and is only a constraint where a gateway enforces it. ``upstream_serves`` is the observation: every tool the upstream offers at the deployed version. State it only where it DIFFERS from the allowlist; absence means the two are identical, which is the normal case for a provider that serves exactly what is allowed. The difference between them measures unenforced exposure, and a provider whose difference is non-empty needs a gateway in front. Plus schema hash and mutation policy."
msgstr "``tools``: ``allowlist`` Je, ni nini msomaji anaweza kufikia na ``writer_allowlist`` Nini mwandishi anaweza kufikia; kupelekwa hutoa mkataba mmoja kwa kila jukumu, kila mmoja na mbeba mlango wake mwenyewe, kwa sababu mlango unawaambia walinganiaji mbali kwa uaminifu na kwa kitu kingine chochote. ``allowlist`` Ni sera, jukwaa gani linaruhusu watumiaji kufikia, na ni kizuizi tu ambapo lango linatekeleza. ``upstream_serves`` Ni uchunguzi: kila chombo cha upstream hutoa katika toleo lililotumika. Sema tu ambapo ni tofauti kutoka kwa ruhusu; kutokuwepo inamaanisha mbili ni sawa, ambayo ni kesi ya kawaida kwa mtoa huduma ambaye hutumikia kile kinachoruhusiwa. Tofauti kati yao hupima mfiduo usio na nguvu, na mtoa huduma ambaye tofauti ni isiyo ya usawa inahitaji lango mbele. Zaidi ya muundo hash na sera ya mabadiliko."

