msgstr ""

msgid "`files/playwright/test-multisite-rbac.js` checks the member's own site with the protocol of the pass's base URL (`:78`, `:92`, `:112`, `:146`): on the Tor pass that is `http://` on an onion base, while own sites exist only on the regular network with TLS (served names get no onion sibling), and the own-site login redirect host at `:159` and the `maxRedirects: 0` POST at `:134-139` expect the onion network. Measured in `/tmp/compose-deploy-iam-20.log`; the SOCKS failure of the same spec is fixed by the served domains in `plugins/lookup/browser_proxy_bypass.py`. Options: render `WORDPRESS_SITE_OWNER_BASE_URL` into `templates/playwright.env.j2` from the served name through `lookup('tls', …)` and check own sites on their own network in every pass, or skip the own-site checks on the Tor pass."
msgstr ""

msgid "`files/playwright/test-native-login-administrator.js:19` failed its first attempt in the B1 compose round of 2026-11-01 on the 60 s wait for `/network` after the sign-in (`files/playwright/_shared.js:90`) and passed on retry (log `/tmp/compose-deploy-iam-15.log:312348`); options: wait for the session cookie and the post-login redirect response instead of the `/network` render, or raise the cause in Friendica's post-login page load first."
msgstr ""

msgid "`files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js` fails on a stack with `seaweedfs` on and `sso` off (measured: `input[type=\"file\"]` never attaches on `/preferences/profile`, 3 of 3 attempts): the action only signs in through Keycloak, so without SSO it stays anonymous and lands on `/login`. Options: sign in through BookWyrm's own `/login` form with the provisioned administrator when `sso` is off, or skip unless `sso` is enabled."
msgstr ""

msgid "`files/playwright/test-smiley-icons.js` exempts `/addon/smiley_pack/icons/opensource/vivaldi.png` (`UPSTREAM_MISSING_ICON`), which the `smiley_pack` addon references but does not ship. The fix PR friendica/friendica-addons#1390 on GitHub was closed unmerged on 2026-11-01 because the repository moved to <https://git.friendi.ca/friendica/friendica-addons>. Open the PR again there (it needs an account on git.friendi.ca; the instance offers OpenID 2.0, which Keycloak does not provide), then put an `upstream:` directive with the new PR URL back above `UPSTREAM_MISSING_ICON`."
