# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`gh api` switches implicitly from GET to POST as soon as a body-flag is present; no explicit `-X`/`--method` is required. Without these ask rules the broad `Bash(*)` allow would let body-carrying `gh api` POSTs through silently. Short forms (`-f`, `-F`), long forms (`--field`, `--raw-field`), and file input (`--input`) are all listed so no spelling slips past. A future gh-CLI body-flag would need to be added here explicitly."
msgstr "`gh api` Inabadilisha kwa urahisi kutoka GET hadi POST haraka kama moto wa mwili uko; hakuna wazi `-X`Kwa hivyo`--method` inapohitajika. Bila ya kuwa na sheria hizi, Bunge `Bash(*)` Kuruhusu mwili kuwaka `gh api` Acha kimya kwa muda. Aina za Shorts (`-f`, Kwa hivyo, `-F`)Aina za muda mrefu (`--field`, Kwa hivyo, `--raw-field`)Kuingia kwa faili (`--input`) Haya yote yanaandikwa kwa hivyo hakuna maandishi ya zamani. Mwili wa gh-CLI unapaswa kuongezwa hapa waziwazi."

# the the the the the the the the the the the the the the the the the the the
# the the the the the the the the the the `gh` Rais afungua ukurasa wa mhariri
# (ya g. `gh issue create` Bila ya `--body`), backdoor iliyocheleweshwa ambayo
# inaishi kikao cha sasa. CLI inayoendelea ni ya uamuzi wa operator wa
# makusudi.
msgid "`gh config set editor /tmp/evil.sh` plants a binary that runs the next time any `gh` subcommand opens an editor (e.g. `gh issue create` without `--body`), a deferred-execution backdoor that survives the current session. Persistent CLI config belongs to a deliberate operator decision."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`gh` CLI's cache directory (HTTP response cache + extension metadata). Granted because every `gh` invocation writes cache entries at startup; denying it would require every `gh` call to be wrapped with an `XDG_CACHE_HOME=/tmp/...` env prefix, which adds a shell shape that falls out of sandbox auto-allow and forces per-subcommand allow entries. Auth tokens are **not** stored here (they live in `~/.config/gh/`, which stays read-only). Persistence trade-off is identical to `~/.cache/pip` / `~/.cache/pre-commit`: cache poisoning, if it occurred, would survive reboots, but API auth is server-side so the blast radius is bounded to wrong-output-to-operator."
msgstr "`gh` Mwongozo wa CLI (Hifadhi ya majibu ya HTTP + ugani wa metadata). Kwa sababu kila mmoja `gh` invocation anaandika entries cache katika mwanzo; kukataa ni lazima kila `gh` Wito kwa kuwa tayari `XDG_CACHE_HOME=/tmp/...` env prefix, ambayo inaongeza sura ya shell kwamba huanguka nje ya sandbox auto-allow na vikosi kwa amri ndogo kuruhusu maingilio. Alama za vidole ni **Sio ya** Imehifadhiwa hapa (wanaishi katika `~/.config/gh/`, ambao bado hawajasoma)Biashara ya kudumu ni sawa na `~/.cache/pip` Kwa hivyo `~/.cache/pre-commit` API Auth ni upande wa seva kwa hivyo radius ya mlipuko imefungwa kwa nje-kwa-operator."

