msgid "`services.matrix.plugins.chatgpt` is the single switch for the AI surface in both flavors: the compose flavor renders `matrix-chatgpt-bot`, the ansible flavor enables `baibot`. Both reach the model through `svc-ai-litellm` with the role's `litellm_api_key`, and MDAD creates the `baibot` account itself from `matrix_user_creator_users_auto`, so no account provisioning step is needed. That account creation runs only under the `ensure-matrix-users-created` tag, which `services.matrix.playbook_tags` carries between `setup-all` and `start`; drop it and baibot starts without an account to log in to. `bootstrap.sh` stops an installed `matrix-synapse.service` before the playbook, and the account creation starts it again on the configuration the playbook has just rendered."
msgstr ""

msgid "`services.matrix.plugins.hookshot` follows the deployment of the partners its connection addons bind, so the bridge comes up wherever `web-app-gitlab` or `web-app-n8n` is deployed. The four `hookshot-*` addons then select which connections MDAD configures through `matrix_bridge_hookshot_<kind>_enabled`; `generic` and `feeds` are upstream defaults the addons drive explicitly. `hookshot-feeds` has no partner service of its own, so enabling it alone does nothing: without `web-app-gitlab` or `web-app-n8n` the bridge it configures is never deployed. Pin it in a round that already carries one of them."
msgstr ""

msgid "`services.mock.enabled` starts a deterministic OpenAI-compatible test upstream from the FreeLLMAPI image and adds it as an extra `customProviders` entry. It answers `/v1/models` and `/v1/chat/completions`, both streaming and non-streaming. It answers a tool request with a call derived from the tool schema, and every other request with `OK`. It needs no key and receives none of the gateway's secrets. The flag is off by default. Only the matrix variant turns it on, so a CI round can route and validate without provider accounts. Production inventories must leave it off."
msgstr ""

